<eSummaryResult><DocSum>
	<Id>200219163</Id>
	<Item Name="Accession" Type="String">GSE219163</Item>
	<Item Name="GDS" Type="String" />
	<Item Name="title" Type="String">CRISPR screens identify gene targets at breast cancer risk loci [ATAC-seq]</Item>
	<Item Name="summary" Type="String">Genome-wide association studies (GWAS) have identified &gt;200 loci associated with breast cancer (BC) risk. The majority of candidate causal variants (CCVs) are in non-coding regions and likely modulate cancer risk by regulating gene expression. However, pinpointing the exact target of the association, and identifying the phenotype it mediates, is a major challenge in the interpretation and translation of GWAS.</Item>
